   "he": "מֵיאֲנָה אוֹ שֶׁחָלְצָה וְכוּ׳. טַעְמָא דְּבֵית דִּין, הָא בִּתְרֵי — לָא,",
   "en": "It is taught in the mishna that if a woman «performed refusal or performed ḥalitza» before a judge, he may still marry her, as he was part of a court. The Gemara deduces from here: «The reason is» specifically that he functioned on «the court» as one of three judges. The Gemara deduces: «Then, if there were» only «two» judges, «he would not» be permitted to marry her."
  }
